# Cross-platform line-ending normalization (Mac · Linux · Windows).
# Without this, Windows checkouts convert to CRLF, making the whole tree
# look modified and breaking determinism golden-hashes. All text is stored
# LF in the repo; binaries are marked so git never touches them.
#
# One-time after adding this file (index free): `git add --renormalize .`

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text types (defensive — code + config + docs stay LF everywhere).
*.rs      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.wgsl    text eol=lf
*.glsl    text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.ron     text eol=lf
*.html    text eol=lf
*.css     text eol=lf
*.ts      text eol=lf
*.js      text eol=lf
*.lua     text eol=lf
*.luau    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep CRLF (some shells require it).
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.ps1     text eol=crlf

# Syntax-aware merge (Mergiraf) — ADR-0107.
# AST-level 3-way merge for the source/config surfaces that concurrent lines
# edit in foundational (two agents adding a variant/field/token in DIFFERENT
# parts of the same file → clean auto-merge instead of a textual conflict).
# Line-merge is tried first; the AST path only runs on the regions that
# actually conflicted. SAFE without the driver configured: git falls back to
# its built-in 3-way merge when `merge=mergiraf` names an unregistered driver
# (so Mac/Windows checkouts without Mergiraf are unaffected). Register the
# driver once per machine with `scripts/mergiraf-setup.sh`.
# NOT a substitute for the tested integration gate — Mergiraf can union code
# that compiles-but-is-wrong; `scripts/foundational-integrate.sh` is what
# proves the combined tree still builds+passes (ADR-0107 Camada 2).
# Cargo.lock (no .toml extension → NOT matched below) and *-registry-init/ are
# regenerated, never hand-merged, on conflict (DIRETRIZ §1.5.5). We deliberately
# leave them on git's DEFAULT merge: it auto-merges disjoint dep/registry
# additions cleanly, and the regen rule is the fallback only when it truly
# conflicts. Forcing them off merge would manufacture conflicts, not prevent them.
*.rs      merge=mergiraf
*.toml    merge=mergiraf
*.json    merge=mergiraf
*.wgsl    merge=mergiraf
*.ron     merge=mergiraf

# Binary assets — never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.webp    binary
*.avif    binary
*.ktx2    binary
*.basis   binary
*.ico     binary
*.icns    binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.wav     binary
*.mp3     binary
*.ogg     binary
*.zip     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.ph2d-vector binary
